===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}

The upper component {{zh-l|*𦉶}} is attested independently in Shang oracle bone script, showing a large {{zh-l|*目|eye}} with a short hooked stroke. Jiang Yubin (蔣玉斌) identifies it as the original character for {{zh-l|*獨|alone}}, while Chen Jian (陳劍) and Guo Yongbing (郭永秉) read it as {{zh-l|*矚|to gaze intently}}, taking the non-{{lang|zh|目}} portion as a figure leaning on a staff. Both words belong to a *dok family associated with focused vision and conspicuousness (cf. {{zh-l|*燭|to illuminate}}). The form with added {{zh-l|*虫|insect}} first appears in Western Zhou inscriptions for the Shu place name; ''{{w|Shuowen Jiezi}}'' reanalyzes it as a {{w|pictogram}} of a silkworm.

